course: dictionary
lesson: 11577
title: Annually means once every year
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Annually means once every year. It is a formal word, so you will often see it in reports, in maths problems and on school notices. Everyday words that mean the same are «every year», «each year» and «a year».
explain: Look at the clues around it. «She earns 30,000 pounds annually.» The word annually tells you the amount is for one year. «The club grows by 10 members annually.» This means the club gets 10 new members every year, and it keeps happening.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it in. «School sports day is held annually» becomes «School sports day is held every year». The sentence still makes sense and means the same, so annually must mean every year.
fact: Annually means once every year.
fact: Annually is an adverb: it tells you how often something happens.
fact: «Annually» can also mean for each year or in a year, as in «she earns 30,000 pounds annually».
fact: In science and geography, you might read about rainfall annually, which means the amount of rain in one year.
fact: Good swaps for annually are «every year», «each year» and «a year».
exercise: «The club grows by 10 members annually.» What does annually mean here? | Once a week | *Once every year | Very quickly | Only once, and never again
exercise: Ella reads, «The school sports day is held annually.» What does this tell her? | It happens only in the morning | It happens every day | It was cancelled | *It happens every year
exercise: Which phrase means the same as annually? | Last week | *Each year | Every day | Once in a blue moon
test: The rain in the town is measured annually. What does annually mean here? | Whenever it rains | Every hour | Only on Sundays | *Once every year
test: Find the word that tells how often: «Our class plants trees annually.» | trees | class | *annually | plants
exam: Maya's teacher says, «Our school trip is held annually.» Maya thinks it happens twice a day. What is the correct meaning of annually? | Only when it is sunny | Twice a day | Every single day | *Once every year
